OxRefine is an independent reimplementation of the OpenRefine data-cleaning
workflow (https://openrefine.org). It reads and writes OpenRefine's operation
history JSON and aims to reproduce OpenRefine's results. OpenRefine is
Copyright (c) 2010 Google Inc. and 2018-present OpenRefine contributors,
licensed under the BSD 3-Clause License. OxRefine contains no OpenRefine code.
Test fixtures under tests/ were produced by running OpenRefine 3.10.1, and the
GREL function descriptions in ui/src/grel-docs.json come from OpenRefine 3.10.1
(get-expression-language-info), used under the same BSD 3-Clause License.

crates/ox-core/assets/commons-codec/ holds the Beider-Morse and Daitch-Mokotoff
rule files from Apache Commons Codec 1.20.0 (the version OpenRefine 3.10.1
uses), under the Apache License 2.0 (LICENSE.txt in that folder):

  Apache Commons Codec
  Copyright 2002-2025 The Apache Software Foundation

  This product includes software developed at
  The Apache Software Foundation (https://www.apache.org/).

crates/ox-core/src/double_metaphone.rs is adapted from rphonetic 4.0.0
(https://github.com/Dalvany/rphonetic, Apache License 2.0), a port of Apache
Commons Codec's DoubleMetaphone; the changes are described at its top.

crates/ox-core/src/metaphone3.rs is adapted from the metaphone3 crate 0.2.0
(https://github.com/kakserpom/metaphone3-rs, MIT License), a port of Lawrence
Philips' Metaphone 3 (BSD License); the changes are described at its top.
